delivery and work vehicles, and port/airport/warehouse and other industrial applications, as well as ride-sharing services; and residential comprising single family homes and multi-family apartments and condominiums customers. ChargePoint Holdings, Inc. was founded in 2007 and is headquartered in Campbell, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Richard  Wilmer | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $625,000 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $286K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $45K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["ChargePoint Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $313M market cap on $411M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -133% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 22% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $67M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -8.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 16% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-3.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 59% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (88% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.125},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 131% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ChargePoint Holdings, Inc. (CHPT) Beats Stock Market Upswing: What Investors Need to Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028253/chargepoint-holdings-inc-chpt-beats-stock-market-upswing-what-investors-need-to-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7